# Excluded from `git archive` output, which is what GitHub serves as a release
# tarball or zip. A clone is unaffected: contributors get these, people who
# download a packaged release do not.
#
# TESTING.md is deliberately NOT here. It is operator-facing -- the step table,
# how to report a failure, the known rough edges -- and belongs in the package.
#
# .gitignore is excluded because it is a git artifact and a release archive is
# not a repository. What it documents for a contributor -- that configs/ and
# docs/ are operator-supplied -- is already said in configs/README.md and
# docs/README.md, both of which do ship.
tests/          export-ignore
CLAUDE.md       export-ignore
.gitattributes  export-ignore
.gitignore      export-ignore
